# Citation metadata for the specsr-roman package.
#
# GitHub renders this as the "Cite this repository" button. The top-level
# block describes the software; `preferred-citation` points at the method
# paper, which is what someone using the approach should cite.
#
# The Roman-specific manuscript is in preparation and its author list is not
# yet confirmed, so it is deliberately not listed here. Add it — with the
# agreed authors — when it is submitted, and keep `version` and
# `date-released` in step with pyproject.toml on every release.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the paper below. To reference a
  specific version of the code, cite this repository directly.
title: "specsr-roman: physics-informed super-resolution of Roman grism spectra"
abstract: >-
  A three-stage, physics-informed deep learning framework that super-resolves
  Roman Space Telescope slitless grism spectra, with a photometry-conditioned
  redshift head that breaks the single-line alias degeneracy and an
  attention-based refinement stage calibrated on line recoverability, so that
  emission lines the data cannot support are not drawn.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Aryana
    family-names: Haghjoo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-3071-7143"
    email: ahagh010@ucr.edu
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Physics and Astronomy, University of California Riverside
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-26"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/aryana-haghjoo/specsr-roman"
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - spectroscopy
  - super-resolution
  - deep-learning
  - roman-space-telescope
  - grism
  - slitless-spectroscopy

references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      The High Latitude Spectroscopic Survey on the Nancy Grace Roman Space
      Telescope
    authors:
      - given-names: Yun
        family-names: Wang
    journal: "The Astrophysical Journal"
    year: 2022
    notes: Roman GRS grism configuration used to disperse and extract.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      OpenUniverse2024: A shared, simulated view of the sky for the next
      generation of cosmological surveys
    authors:
      - given-names: Michael A.
        family-names: Troxel
    year: 2025
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:2501.05632"
        description: arXiv preprint
    notes: Source of the simulated images, catalogues and SEDs.

